 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.06666666666666667,
   "dur": 4.267,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Is a tan a shield? A thin one, built after the harm."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.433333333333334,
   "dur": 10.333,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Sunlight carries ultraviolet, and its shorter rays reach the living cells under the dead layer. In under a trillionth of a second, one can fuse two letters of their DNA."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 16.633333333333333,
   "dur": 8.543,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "The cell notices. A guardian protein switches on, and the cell sends a chemical message down to the pigment cells: make melanin."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 26.433333333333334,
   "dur": 10.057,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "In Boston, mice whose skin cells lacked that guardian never tanned at all. So a tan isn't skin getting ready for the sun. It's skin answering damage already done."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 39.03333333333333,
   "dur": 9.613,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Over the next few days, the melanin settles over each nucleus like a tiny parasol. Together, a whole tan adds up to about SPF three or four."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 52.56666666666667,
   "dur": 7.306,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "Each parasol is about as wide as its nucleus: a dozen side by side would span a sheet of paper."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 60.96666666666667,
   "dur": 5.446,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "So, is a tan a shield? A thin one. It's how your skin remembers the light."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 67.5,
   "dur": 4.254,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: who has more pigment cells, the darkest skin or the lightest?"
  }
 ]
}